// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`tools/list every tool has a description of its fields and an outputSchema 1`] = `
[
  {
    "_meta": {
      "class": "push",
    },
    "description": "Request a push to branch agent/<session-id>, or agent/<session-id>-<branch> when \`branch\` is given. \`repository_id\` names the repository to push to: an attached repository, or, omitted, the session's own. \`source_ref\` names the local branch of the workspace (for example \`guard-docs\`) whose latest commit is pushed; without it the commit the workspace is on is pushed. Only commits are pushed, never uncommitted edits. One call pushes one repository: for several repositories, each repository's change sits on its own local branch, started from that repository's \`<repository_id>/<branch>\` (\`origin/<branch>\` for the session's own repository), and each call carries its \`repository_id\` and \`source_ref\` (a branch that shares no history with the target's default branch is refused as \`unrelated_history\`; an existing target branch gives \`non_fast_forward\` instead). Once two pushes are asked for, every one needs its \`source_ref\`: a call refused as \`source_ref_required\` names the target that lacks one in \`details.target_branch\`, and the same call with a \`source_ref\` is accepted. With the installation's agent action flows on, the answer is \`deferred\` with \`push_intent_id\`: the platform makes the push request when the reply ends, and \`open_pull_request\` accepts that \`push_intent_id\` at once, also while the push waits for approval. A push waits for a person's approval when the release requires one, and its pull request opens once the push succeeds. With the flows off, \`source_ref\` is refused as \`source_ref_unsupported\`, the commit the workspace was on when it was last saved is pushed, and the push request is returned, or \`deferred\` when nothing is saved yet. \`pull_request\` is not accepted: a call that carries it is refused with \`pull_request_needs_tool_call\` and nothing is created; the pull request is opened by \`open_pull_request\` with the \`push_intent_id\` this tool returns.",
