  {
    "_meta": {
      "class": "pull_request.write",
    },
    "description": "Open, or return the already open, pull request from the branch and commit of a pushed push request (\`push_request_id\`), or, with the installation's agent action flows on, schedule it with \`push_intent_id\` (or a push request that is not pushed yet): \`scheduled\` means the platform opens it once the push finishes, with the content of the first call. With the flows off, a push request that is not pushed yet is refused with \`not_pushed\`. A pull request already open for the branch on another commit than the pushed one is refused with \`head_moved\` and not adopted. Content fields: \`title\`; \`summary\` (what changed and why, a few sentences); \`changes\` (one change per item); \`rationale\` (the reason for the change); \`testing\` (how it was checked); \`notes\` (what a reviewer needs to know); \`related\` (issues: \`number\`, optional \`repository_id\`, \`closes\` to close it on merge). \`body\` is the legacy single text and cannot be combined with the fields above.",
